From 609c4f1de8e6228c6c91b261e8484ddf0297fb35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:37:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sherlock-lfr: T9 decoder with every T4 check; 5-pair lane
 map; T10a call run

- iface.rs: STMT 116 and 5 lane-map pairs (O7, 12,166 L words);
  decode_with(keys, sibs): X Canon and pinned, layout_d pinned (ENC-3),
  opening-proof form of R (DIGEST(SHK_SET) at entry 4), lane map off
  lanes 0 and 1, the N-11 prologue (template lanes 2 to 9, popeq lane
  10 = a_in; chunk anchor write lanes 11 to 21, lane 20 = a_out), PATH
  replay with wrap-private siblings; Case::Open; reservation_with
  (anchor_d2 for a ledger anchor); unit tests for every check.
- lverify.rs gen_r_check: the opening-proof form of R on the L_Fr tape.
- iface_fixture, j5_gate: the open case (seed 18).
- lfr_e3: the T9 named mutants and the open, chunk and PATH positives,
  keys in the decode section; enc_wrap, fp8_keyset: keys in the doc.
- lfr_call: the acceptRun run of sherlock-ledger.compact (X = the
  cached-trace commitment of L, ledger anchor C_L, 4 PUB entries, 5-pair
  lane map), args mode with a native decode of a real call vector.
